    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register table prints both a PDU (wire) address and a logical address (PDU + 40001 for holding registers). 'documented' holds the logical number; the PDU number is what goes in the request, e.g. logical 40101 = PDU 100."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "V1.03 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "TDO340 User manual",
    "doc_number": "Revision R1.2",
    "revision_date": "2026-10",
    "url": "https://www.teracomsystems.com/download/tdo340-modbus-rtu-relay-output-module/",
    "pages": "pp. 5-7 (Modbus address table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are taken from the manual's PDU address column (0-based); the logical column adds 40001 for holding registers and 1 for coils (discrete outputs), as the manual states.",
    "Left out: the 32-bit float/integer test-value registers (PDU 82-95), which only exist to check word order; the 16-bit test values are kept.",
    "Coils run from PDU 1 (logical 2) to PDU 4 (logical 5) for relays 1-4, exactly as the table prints them; there is no relay at coil 0.",
    "This model has no Data order register and no 32-bit measurement values."
  ],
